### Shell Execution Rules
- Do not chain commands with `&&`, `;`, or `|` when individual tool calls can be made.
- Do not use command substitutions like `$(cmd)`. Run the inner command first, then use the literal result.
- Avoid wrappers (`sudo`, `eval`). Call target binaries directly so commands remain auto-approvable.
- Write temporary/scratch files (including PR body drafts and commit message files) under `<worktree>/.scratch/` rather than `/tmp`.

